course: dictionary
lesson: 10396
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Tribe is a good example. In history, a tribe is a group of families and people who share the same ancestors, language, customs and way of life, often with their own leader.
explain: In the Bible, «the twelve tribes» means the family groups said to come from the twelve sons of Jacob. The words around the word show you which meaning is meant.
explain: In everyday talk, a tribe can be any big group who belong together or like the same things. «A tribe of kids» means many children, not a family group at all. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, then pick the meaning that fits.
fact: A tribe is a group of families and people who share ancestors, language, customs and a way of life.
fact: Tribes of ancient Britain, Native American nations and First Nations, Aboriginal peoples, and Māori iwi are studied in history and geography.
fact: «Tribal» is the adjective, as in tribal customs.
fact: In biology, a tribe is a group of related plants or animals.
fact: In everyday talk, «a tribe of» can mean a large number of people, especially children.
exercise: «Temujin united the Mongol tribes.» In this sentence, what is a tribe? | A group of fans who like the same band | A group of plants or animals | A kind of ladder | *A group of families and people who share customs and a way of life, often with a leader
exercise: In the Bible, «the twelve tribes» came from whom? | Twelve plants in a garden | *The twelve sons of Jacob | Twelve chiefs of ancient Britain | Twelve kings in London
exercise: Ella says, «There's a tribe of kids in the park.» What does she mean? | One very tall child | A family of chiefs with grand titles | *A large group of children | A group of related plants
test:
«The fans formed a tribe that followed the band everywhere.» Which meaning fits best? | A family from ancient Britain | *A big group of people who like the same thing | A group of related plants or animals | The twelve sons of Jacob
In biology, what is a tribe? | *A group of related plants or animals | A group of families with a leader | A ladder to heaven | A title given to a chief
exam:
In «Kipling lists the Tribe's chiefs with grand, funny titles», what does Tribe mean? | *A group of families and people who share customs and often have a leader | A group of related plants | A bunch of fans at a concert | A pile of bricks
